    <fr:route>/def-0027/</fr:route>
    <fr:title text="Polynomial">Polynomial</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    A function <fr:tex display="inline">f: R \to  R</fr:tex> is a <html:strong>polynomial</html:strong> with coefficients in ring <fr:tex display="inline">R</fr:tex> if
    there exists  <fr:tex display="inline">n \in  \N </fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline">a_0, a_1, \ldots , a_n \in  R</fr:tex> such that
    <fr:tex display="block">
        f(x) = a_0 + a_1 x + a_2 x^2 + \cdots  + a_n x^n
    </fr:tex>
    for all <fr:tex display="inline">x \in  R</fr:tex>. We denote the set all polynomials with coefficients in <fr:tex display="inline">R</fr:tex> by <fr:tex display="inline">\mathcal {P}(R)</fr:tex>.
</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
